<title>BELGIUM: Belgium urges nationals to quit east Zaire.</title>
<headline>Belgium urges nationals to quit east Zaire.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium has urged its nationals to leave in eastern Zaire because of the fighting there between ethnic Tutsis and Zairean troops, Belga news agency reported on Friday.</p>
<p>The agency, citing Foreign Ministry sources, also said a diplomat from Belgium's Kinshasha embassy would go to assess the situation in the region, where an estimated 300 Belgians live.</p>
</text>
